title The front door lifted out of seventy-nine rungs at once
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, deep-read council-rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment.
think Read the running thread first. The last three laps read rota rows 4, 0, and 1, so this lap reads row 2 -- Fire and Mars, cut and stop: Standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal. Standfast ordered the reds ahead of everything, so the ledger came before the crux.
think The ledger is clean. Rows %125 and %126 both closed on metal last lap, and reds_ledger_monotone_witness runs GREEN at rows=126 with gaps_or_dupes=0 -- the guard whose equality became a floor the same lap it was booked. No open agent-closable red stands, so the line moves.
think The crux was named, measured, and unblocked. main at 64 rungs by 17 lines led the Caravan lift arc twice over -- third on the carry queue by weight, and first on the ceiling, with five lines of headroom left under 87,800. Last lap surveyed it fully and could not lift it, because asking four base modules to import their own harness segfaulted the Rye bridge; that compiler fault is fixed, so the door was open.
think Measured the cohorts rather than trusting the survey. Hashing every main body across the 110 modules answers exactly: 64 identical, then 15 more differing in one qualifier -- cohort.run_dependent where the 64 write run_dependent -- and eighteen singletons that are genuinely their own. So one lifted body serves 79 rather than 64, and the widening is what erases the qualifier.
think The lift is the harness pattern the ladder already runs. run_main takes the rung as a comptime parameter and reaches run_dependent, run_self_test, and fixed_argv_words through it, so one body runs against whichever rung handed itself in. The 64 publish the run_dependent they already wrote; the 15 seat pub const run_dependent = cohort.run_dependent, which is the qualifier made a name.
think Priced the widening before taking it. Publishing run_self_test across 79 files and run_dependent across 62 costs zero carried lines -- a keyword, never a body -- which is the fold-pays-its-successors argument the scan already records. Thirty-five rungs needed the harness import added; forty-four already had it.
obs The build found the widening I had not measured. Ten rungs declared fixed_argv_words privately rather than pub, and the compiler named the first one by file and line the moment the lifted body reached for it. Three symbols form the contract and I had checked two -- the third was uniform in the two files I read by hand and non-uniform across the arc. Measurement beats memory holds even when the memory is a sample of two.
obs The two readings are what make this a fold rather than a cost moved somewhere cheaper to count. Carry falls 87,795 to 86,774, a thousand and twenty-one lines, while delegates rise 2,365 to 2,444 -- exactly the seventy-nine stubs that replaced the bodies. A fold that traded a large family for a large delegate count would show both numbers moving together; these move apart by more than twelve to one.
obs main has left the fold queue entirely. The top twelve now open on seat_the_history at 1,152 and seat_the_record at 1,080, with read_the_finding at 1,045 stepping up into third where main stood. The ceiling comes down 87,800 to 86,780, handing back the room the fold won and keeping the same six lines of headroom the discipline has held all along.
obs This is the widest single fold the ladder has taken -- seventy-nine rungs against the previous high of forty-three -- and it was the cheapest, because the door is seventeen lines rather than a hundred and thirty-seven. Width and depth are independent, and the queue is sorted by their product, so the widest fold was never the one at the top of the list.
obs The rota row shaped the ordering rather than decorating it. Standfast says stop for a red before new work; the ledger was clean, so the answer was to proceed, which is the discipline working rather than skipped. The three depths of removal named what this lap is: a lift is not a cut at all -- nothing left the tree that was not byte-identical to something that stayed -- so no cairn is owed and none was taken.
